{"name":"Blue Heron","hex":"#939ec5","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue heron","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of great blue heron.","Synonym of little blue heron."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_heron"}],"entries":[{"title":"Great blue heron","blocks":[{"text":"The great blue heron is a large wading bird in the heron family (Ardeidae), common near shores of open water and wetlands over most of North and Central America, as well as Northwestern South America, the Caribbean, and the Galápagos Islands. It is occasionally found in the Azores and is a rare vagrant to Europe. An all-white population found in South Florida, the Florida Keys, and the Caribbean islands, is known as the great white heron. Debate exists about whether these white birds are a color morph of the great blue heron, a subspecies of it, or an entirely separate species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/GreatBlueHeronInARiver.jpg/330px-GreatBlueHeronInARiver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_blue_heron","wikidata":"Q333796"},{"title":"Little blue heron","blocks":[{"text":"The little blue heron is a small heron of the genus Egretta. It is a small, darkly colored heron with a two-toned bill. Juveniles are entirely white, bearing resemblance to the snowy egret. During the breeding season, adults develop different coloration on the head, legs, and feet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Little_Blue_Fly-By.png/330px-Little_Blue_Fly-By.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_blue_heron","wikidata":"Q371028"},{"title":"Blue Heron (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Heron is a 2025 drama film written and directed by Sophy Romvari, in her feature-length film directorial debut. The film, a Canadian-Hungarian co-production, is based in part on Romvari's own childhood and her previous short film Still Processing. It stars Eylul Guven as Sasha, the eight-year-old daughter of a Hungarian immigrant family who relocate to Vancouver Island in the late 1990s while their oldest son Jeremy displays increasingly dangerous behavioural issues in their new environment. The cast also includes Ádám Tompa and Iringó Réti as Sasha's parents, Liam Serg and Preston Drabble as Sasha's brothers, and Amy Zimmer as adult Sasha."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fe/Blue_Heron_%28film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Heron_(film)","wikidata":"Q135321336"},{"title":"Heron","blocks":[{"text":"Herons are long-legged, long-necked, freshwater and coastal birds in the family Ardeidae, with 75 recognised species, some of which are referred to as egrets or bitterns rather than herons. Members of the genus Botaurus are referred to as bitterns, and, together with the zigzag heron, or zigzag bittern, in the monotypic genus Zebrilus, form a monophyletic group, Botaurinae, within the Ardeidae family. Egrets do not form a biologically distinct group from herons, and tend to be named differently because they are mainly white or have decorative plumes in breeding plumage. Herons, by evolutionary adaptation, have long beaks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Ardeidae-01.jpg/330px-Ardeidae-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heron","wikidata":"Q18789"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Great_blue_heron_%28Ardea_herodias_occidentalis%29_white_form.JPG/500px-Great_blue_heron_%28Ardea_herodias_occidentalis%29_white_form.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Great_blue_heron_%28Ardea_herodias_occidentalis%29_white_form.JPG/1280px-Great_blue_heron_%28Ardea_herodias_occidentalis%29_white_form.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Great_blue_heron_%28Ardea_herodias_occidentalis%29_white_form.JPG/500px-Great_blue_heron_%28Ardea_herodias_occidentalis%29_white_form.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreat_blue_heron_(Ardea_herodias_occidentalis)_white_form.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Great_Blue_Heron_%289012933612%29.jpg/500px-Great_Blue_Heron_%289012933612%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Great_Blue_Heron_%289012933612%29.jpg/1280px-Great_Blue_Heron_%289012933612%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Great_Blue_Heron_%289012933612%29.jpg/500px-Great_Blue_Heron_%289012933612%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreat_Blue_Heron_(9012933612).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Blue_Heron%2C_Lake_Sammamish_State_Park.jpg/500px-Blue_Heron%2C_Lake_Sammamish_State_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Blue_Heron%2C_Lake_Sammamish_State_Park.jpg/1280px-Blue_Heron%2C_Lake_Sammamish_State_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Blue_Heron%2C_Lake_Sammamish_State_Park.jpg/500px-Blue_Heron%2C_Lake_Sammamish_State_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u